    "created_at": "2022-08-26T18:04:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-26T18:04:07Z",
    "body": "Would it be reasonable to expose the total number of pre-decompression bytes received so far? Something like `response.body.receivedBytes`, which would give the number of bytes received over the wire, which would be directly comparable to the `Content-Length` value.\r\n\r\nAs far as I know, it is not always possible to compute the expected total uncompressed payload size. With Content-Encoding: gzip it might be possible after receiving the gzip header, but it is not possible with Content-Encoding: deflate.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
